        "original_id": "574f13b4-7828-56a7-b3f8-b57df9476281",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: One Magic Christmas, Muppet Treasure Island, Life Begins at Eight-thirty, The Christmas That Almost Wasn't, Trading Places, I'll Be Home for Christmas, Elf\n- People: Phillip Borsos, Robert Louis Stevenson, Monty Woolley, Alberto Rabagliati, Dan Aykroyd, Jan Rubes, David Huddleston, Jonathan Taylor Thomas, Ed Asner, Bill Barretta\n- Topics: Santa Claus in film, principal puppeteers\n\nFacts:\n- In 1942, Monty Woolley portrayed Santa Claus in the film \"Life Begins at Eight-thirty.\"\n- In 1966, Alberto Rabagliati portrayed Santa Claus in the film \"The Christmas That Almost Wasn't.\"\n- In 1983, Dan Aykroyd portrayed Santa Claus in the film \"Trading Places.\"\n- In 1985, \"One Magic Christmas\" was released as an American/Canadian Christmas fantasy film directed by Phillip Borsos.\n- In 1985, Jan Rubes portrayed Santa Claus in \"One Magic Christmas.\"\n- In 1985, David Huddleston portrayed Santa Claus in a film whose title is blank in the source text.\n- In 1996, \"Muppet Treasure Island\" was released as an American musical adventure comedy film based on Robert Louis Stevenson's \"Treasure Island.\"\n- In 1996, Bill Barretta made his film debut as a principal puppeteer in \"Muppet Treasure Island\" as Clueless Morgan.\n- In 1998, Jonathan Taylor Thomas portrayed Santa Claus in \"I'll Be Home for Christmas.\"\n- In 2003, Ed Asner portrayed Santa Claus in the film \"Elf.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
